P-5: spec 004's amendments to the arrival check (tasks.md T036; contracts/intake-amendments.md §7; FR-015, FR-023,
FR-077 items 3 and 4). Made on feat/004-intake, and regenerated on feat/004-intake-r2 against main's four files as
a964494 has them, unchanged at main 130d011 (P-1 to P-4 applied); apply after M8, then the P-6 commit, P-7, and P-8
(docs/merge-requests/2026-10-30-feat-004-intake-r2.md). git apply skips this header.

    T031 is settled (2026-10-30). MARK_HUMAN, the mark of a file whose record's steps are all by hand, is IPTC's
    digitalCreation, "Media created by a human using non-generative tools", which replaced digitalArt on 2024-09-17
    (cv.iptc.org/newscodes/digitalsourcetype/). The patch adds it as one line of tools/gates/arrival_check.py:

        +MARK_HUMAN = "digitalCreation"

It changes four files:
- tools/gates/arrival_check.py: M5 (C1, the mark the record's steps call for, and trainedAlgorithmicMedia alone
  under assets/twin/ and docs/research/images/), R1 (C2, design), P2 (C4, screens_plain_live_face, true or
  not_applicable), P1 (C5, likeness_accepted not_applicable for a room file with no likeness; spec 003's breadth
  otherwise, with a WARN line, which fails nothing, for a hand-made or composite file outside it that the changes
  being checked add or change), F3 (C6, every room file at gzip-9, phase 3 once assets/room/ holds one), F2 (C7,
  per_asset.room's six keys, exit 2 otherwise), and AMENDMENTS = ("004-C1", "004-C2", "004-C4", "004-C5", "004-C6",
  "004-C7").
- tools/gates/test/test_arrival_check.py and tools/gates/test/arrival_fixtures.py: §7's cases, built at run time.
- tools/gates/test/test_run_checks.py: one case, make check reading the arrival check's WARN line as PASS.

Regenerated after T041's review (part 1, I1 and nit 5) and its re-review (part 1): P1 then asked main's approval of
any file whose record's steps call for a mark but trainedAlgorithmicMedia, wherever it lives, and R4 had such a
record name it; a non-room kind under assets/room/ is tested against P1, P2, and F2.

Regenerated again on feat/004-intake-r2, after the Author's answers of 2026-10-30: T031 settled, the term unchanged;
and I1's hardening withdrawn, on his answer "No, let's relax that with a warning of saying it's up to the contributor
to check for likeness. Deprecate the heavy check." P1 and R4 again ask only for a room file, the twin's, a likeness,
or a photo source. A hand-made or composite file outside them passes with one line, which no exit code counts:

    WARN <path>: its record's steps call for the hand-made mark, and the file needs no approval, so it's up to the
    contributor to check for likeness (spec 004, Amendment C1)

Spec 003's R7 case keeps the composite mark its steps call for, with no approval.

And after that branch's review (APPROVE with fixes): the line names only a file the changes being checked add or
change, the staged files, each walked commit's, or the named paths. The last pass over a tip's whole tree records
none, so a file main already holds isn't named again at every later gate (N-1). Pinned besides: per_asset.room with
small_props [], the Author's P-6, holding no texture to its side while the other caps hold; and make check's
run_checks.py reading the WARN line as PASS (N-5). The gate's own classify reads the same three prefixes; its tests
are P-10's file, so this patch leaves it alone.

